Test Case ID: TC-UM-02
Test Component: Admin Role Boundary & Visibility Restrictions
Test Description: Verify that regular Admin users are strictly restricted from viewing, editing, or modifying any Superadmin accounts within the system.
Test Steps:
-Log in using credentials associated with a standard Admin role (non-superadmin).
-Access the User Management directory list and inspect visible user records.
-Verify that all Superadmin accounts are completely hidden from the list view.
-Attempt to access or modify a Superadmin profile via direct URL navigation or API calls, and verify that the request is rejected with a forbidden (403) status.
Expected Result: Regular administrators have zero visibility or editing access over Superadmin accounts, maintaining strict hierarchical boundaries.
Status: PASS ✅

Test Case ID: TC-UM-03
Test Component: Last-Superadmin System Safety Guard
Test Description: Verify that the system strictly prevents the deletion, blocking, or demotion of the last remaining Superadmin account.
Test Steps:
-Set up a test environment state where exactly one active Superadmin account exists.
-Attempt to block, delete, or demote this sole remaining Superadmin account through the management interface or backend action.
-Observe system behavior and inspect error handling responses.
-Verify that the safety guard blocks the transaction and displays an explicit error warning (e.g., "Cannot remove the final Superadmin").
Expected Result: The system enforces the last-superadmin guardrail successfully, preventing accidental lockout or loss of top-level administrative control.
Status: PASS ✅